@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Litware
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Go-live | 2027-W11 (status `onboarding` in the registry until the account team moves it to live) |
+| Contract | `docs/LITWARE_SOW.md` |
+| Grain / timezone | 20 minutes / Europe/London |
+| Operating hours | 07:00–21:00 local, seven days; email contacts 07:00–19:00, nobody on email before 09:00 |
+| Queues | priority, standard, email |
+| Config | `configs/litware.yaml` (schema 1) |
+| Roster | `data/agents/litware.csv`, 24 agents (6 part-time) |
+| Data | `data/litware/export_<ISO>.csv`, local time stamped at the interval END, UTC offset per row (`data/litware/README.txt`) |
+
+## Run
+
+`python -m wfm run --client litware --week <week>` writes `schedule.csv`, `eval.json`, `RUNBOOK.md` and
+`exceptions.md` under `out/litware/` (about 30 s). The RUNBOOK's handover note comes from
+`docs/clients/litware_handover.md`.
+
+## Exceptions (SOW §2.6)
+
+Email intervals between 07:00 and 09:00 local that need agents cannot be staffed (§2.5), so they are listed
+under `## Exceptions` in the RUNBOOK (start in UTC), kept in required hours, and left out of attainment and
+of `understaffed_interval_hours`. `wfm/infeasible.py` also lists any interval needing more agents than hold
+the skill. `exceptions.md` (§2.7) records any weekly target missed with the roster.
